Only the antisymmetric part of the edge product contributes. Defining the oriented area bivector $\Sigma^{\mu\nu}
  =
  \epsilon^\mu\eta^\nu-\epsilon^\nu\eta^\mu,$ we may equivalently write $\Delta V^\alpha
  =
  \frac12
  R^\alpha{}_{\beta\mu\nu}
  V^\beta\Sigma^{\mu\nu}
  +
  O(\ell^3).$

