p.src:
In the product of two four-velocity components, the dominant term is therefore the $00$ term. For a spatial index $i$, $\frac{d^2x^i}{dt^2}
  \simeq
  -\Gamma^i{}_{00}.$ The connection is not itself a tensor, but in this chosen weak-field frame this component is the relativistic expression that reduces to the Newtonian acceleration field.

