p.src:
Expand the relevant connection: $\Gamma^i{}_{00}
  =
  \frac12 g^{i\rho}
  \left(
    2\partial_0g_{\rho0}
    -
    \partial_\rho g_{00}
  \right).$ The derivatives of the Minkowski part vanish, so every derivative in this expression is already first order in $h_{\mu\nu}$. Replacing the outside inverse metric by $\eta^{\mu\nu}$ is therefore consistent: including its $O(h)$ correction would produce only $O(h^2)$ terms.

