p.src:
The slowly varying source assumption makes the time derivatives $\partial_0g_{\rho0}$ negligible. Since $\eta^{ij}=-\delta^{ij}$, we obtain $\Gamma^i{}_{00}
  \simeq
  \frac12\delta^{ij}\partial_jg_{00},$ and hence $\boxed{
  \frac{d^2x^i}{dt^2}
  \simeq
  -\frac12\delta^{ij}\partial_jg_{00}.}$

