The live sign bookkeeping pauses several times here, and rightly so: with signature $+---$, losing one minus sign would turn attractive gravity into repulsive gravity. Keeping the metric convention explicit settles the result. Newtonian motion obeys $\frac{d^2x^i}{dt^2}
  =
  -\delta^{ij}\partial_j\Phi.$ Comparing Eqs.  and  gives $\partial_i g_{00}=2\partial_i\Phi.$

